{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact head f8d8980a82e9a3e739430ee2e33d4292085eece0. One P2 remains in the public integrity-mode description. The two selected shipped tests pass, and the earlier mode and legacy-decoder repairs remain supported. This verdict binds only intermediate-verifier request 42342e35a7660b466b3f623309702461e8f44f6f / builder promise 4e66accc560de6f8ca320ee24593cb0df4f63448. It does not close original Stage 3 or Stage 4.\n\nReview identity and provenance\n\nInvitation: 43172fc4f66def3e0bf4bd02a178de0bb6d1f186. Checker promise: b9b547f1f1ae00e9293883c1abbf0579d853f59f. Primary: b10b2c724dfaeb0db46bdf9034be4486f4cd62a1 (plans/README.md). All 47 invited artifacts are supplied, with the primary first. The producer listed it last; reordering changes no provenance. Normal review preparation assigns the sole original 42342e35 / 4e66accc implementation binding.\n\nRoot independently checked all 47 exact Git blob identities, byte lengths, SHA-256 digests, retained source copies, raw immutable event bases and event trees. All direct artifact bases are the sole 4e66accc promise. All artifact event trees contain only event; the source copies are Git-object evidence, not embedded artifact attachments. The agent's final metadata at frontier 15189 has all 47 effective, nonretired and nonstale, with 46 succession-unrecorded signals preserved as metadata. Those signals do not establish succession or source approval. The complete raw invitation and primary-first list match.\n\nThe path set is identical to f258: 40 unchanged and seven changed artifacts, totaling 2,269,074 bytes. Root checked all 738 archived source identities against actual f8 Git blobs and all 942 source evidence seals. The full f258→f8 delta is 27 paths: five verifier paths, the shared ledger, a separate package invariant row, three Stage 5 paths and 17 package-repair paths. The complete 6b→f8 delta is six paths: five verifier paths and the ledger. Neither composition comparison grants approval to another lane. Source and identity report: /tmp/artroom-checker-verifier-f8-source-awyij2x1/report.md, SHA-256 7fb3b1d8e516dc8fd61908edfaba394f319894dc2aacff5c651d6cc27ef0c6e4; manifest SHA-256 9b48c3eeb0764787070c42af7573b160733ee87ae815a54b250cf5a044c59418.\n\nP2 — disclose the limited retained-context/Git comparison\n\npackages/log/src/verify.ts:296, mirrored at plans/README.md:3438, says: “This run compared no recorded context with Git objects, so it claims no Git witness.” The categorical comparison denial is inaccurate. This is a source-qualified finding; there is no new runtime countercase for this comparison in this review.\n\nThe compared list belongs to the recorded evaluator context. packages/contract/src/policy.ts:352–391 defines ReplayContext and Decision.input as its canonical JSON digest, including rule input and budget; PolicyProposal at :189–196 includes base and changed. The evaluator owns that context (packages/policy/src/context.ts:47–51), hashes it (rules.ts:93–102), records the digest with the same context (:133–135), and Room retains its canonical bytes under that digest (packages/room/src/core.ts:920–921).\n\nverify.ts:453–477 checks retained publication/digests and decodes input objects; lookup :505–512 returns that decoded context, possibly through the existing cache. decode.ts:481–520 checks strict UTF-8/JSON, context kind and input/budget object shapes. This supplies digest-addressed context bytes, not proof that every semantic field agrees with a rebuilt context.\n\nwitnessOf at verify.ts:645–654 obtains that context through lookup and reads input.proposal.base and input.proposal.changed. It obtains actual Git changes at :656. With objects available, :661 calls missingChanges(from.changed, git) and :662 selects Git's list when the retained list omitted a Git change. fold.ts:516–521 compares status/path/renamed-from identities. This happens before policy replay: declared version :1454 and land resolution :1457 precede the