still reports partial carry accounting and the unavailable complete pass boundary/order evidence. CLI text and JSON consume the common report; there was no fresh f8 CLI process here.\n\nOne independent process ran the exact unmodified shipped declared-obligations test file at f8, selecting its mode and admin/ordinary tests: 32 loaded, two passed, zero failed, 30 skipped; exit 0, 0.82252125 seconds, Node 26.10.0 / Vitest 4.1.11. The source/test fixtures and exact command, sanitized environment, output and selected Vitest report were read. There was no separate compile, build, install, full gate, source control or private comparison probe.\n\nThe mode test checks the resealed extra carry judgment: full rejects decision-extra at entry 25 with verified prefix 24 and partial accounting; integrity accepts through 25 with zero replayed decisions and none accounting. Its passive delegated Git reader checks proposal-head reads. The paired guard test rejects the forged admin land at entry 102 with prefix 101 and obl_admin-approval, while the ordinary-rule forgery passes integrity and fails full at entry 93 with obl_tests. Credit is for those actual unmodified shipped assertions. No separate raw forged-log, API-report or read-list artifact was emitted, and no independent signature-verification claim is added for this process.\n\nRuntime report: /tmp/artroom-checker-verifier-f8-runtime-pkmertp5/report.md. Manifest SHA-256 40934afcac82168911367887bc5c6e091d43b18f237184caa878f7306cc4e9c1. Root checked all 18 evidence seals and all 738 before/after/restored source identities against f8 Git objects. Shared dependencies were reused with aliases pointing at the exact fixture; no installation occurred. These passing tests do not establish the disputed categorical comparison statement.\n\nCarried evidence and limits\n\nRoot checked the 17 legacy/decoder support identities against both f258 and f8. The 70,219-byte verify.ts suffix from const empty through EOF is byte-identical, SHA-256 